cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: "CBPL-kit: a web-based interactive toolkit for ternary phase equilibrium and liquid-liquid extraction"
abstract: >-
  CBPL-kit turns the measurements students take in a liquid-liquid extraction
  experiment into a quantitative and reproducible analysis. The Hunter–Nash
  construction, normally carried out by hand on the ternary phase diagram, is
  performed numerically, so an operating condition can be changed and the result
  seen immediately rather than redrawn from scratch. From raw equilibrium and
  tie-line data it fits the binodal curve, constructs the conjugate curve and
  estimates the plait point, and checks tie-line consistency; from a student's
  own run it steps off the equilibrium stages and verifies the mass balance by
  the lever rule. The application runs entirely in the browser through Pyodide,
  requiring no installation, account, or server-side computation, and the same
  Python modules can be imported in a notebook.
